Bugfix: Name the icon-only buttons in the CORS and group settings

Three buttons of the settings UI carried their meaning in a CSS background image
alone. All three are input elements with an empty value attribute, and for that
element type value is the accessible name - an input has no element content that
could supply one instead. Screen readers announced an unnamed button and voice
control could not address them at all.

Filling value was not an option: it is also the visible label text, and both
buttons are constrained to fixed edge lengths of 25 by 30 and 32 by 32 pixels,
so a text value would overflow or be clipped. They now carry an aria-label with
the already translated function name, which leaves the rendering untouched.

The minified sibling of the CORS panel script is updated along with the source,
because that is the file served in production.

WCAG 2.1 AA, SC 4.1.2
